Forget the GL library once glTerm() has closed it.

glTerm() dlcloses libGLESv2 (and libEGL) but leaves the handles set, and _glLoad() only opens them
when they are null. So once the engine has been terminated, the next glInit() -- a second App in the
same process using the GL engine -- looks functions up in a library it has already closed,
and crashes in dlsym.

--- a/src/renderer/gpu_engine/gl/tvgGl.cpp
+++ b/src/renderer/gpu_engine/gl/tvgGl.cpp
@@ -890,8 +890,10 @@
     #endif
 #else
     if (_libGL) dlclose(_libGL);
+    _libGL = nullptr;
     #if defined(THORVG_GL_TARGET_GLES)
         if (_libEGL) dlclose(_libEGL);
+        _libEGL = nullptr;
     #endif
 #endif
 
